On Friday afternoon I take a quiet walk in the sun.
I am carrying my heavy winter coat.
I do not need it at all anymore.
I stop in front of the local dry cleaner.
I open the door and go inside.
It smells of clean clothes and soap in the little shop.
An older man is standing behind the counter.
"Hello, I would like to have this coat cleaned," I say.
I hand the large jacket over the counter.
"Of course," the man answers and examines the fabric.
"It will be ready on Wednesday," he says.
"That will be two hundred and fifty kroner."
I take my debit card out of my bag.
I pay at the register and get a small yellow receipt.
"Thank you very much, have a good weekend," I say.
"You too," he answers with a smile.
I put the receipt down into my bag.
Then I step out onto the busy pavement again.
I enjoy walking in the warm afternoon sun.
